_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 92
---
order: 92
---
short_label: X.92
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If an area is contained by a rational straight line and a second apotome, then the side of the area is a first apotome of a medial straight line.
----
proof:

Let the area {AB} be contained by the rational straight line {AC} and the second apotome {AD}.

I say that the side of the area {AB} is a first apotome of a medial straight line.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="410" height="190" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.92 diagram" src="propX92.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the area AB (ACBD) on the rational AC and the second
    // apotome AD with its annex DG, bisected at E, F from the application to
    // AG; the parallels EH, FI, GK; and the squares LM (RMPL) and NO (PNQO)
    // about the diameter PR, with the gnomon UVW. Added, all hidden at rest:
    // faceless, strokeless twins AB, AI, FK, DH, EK, DK, AK, LM, NO, MN, LO,
    // TS, and the hexagon UVWg for the gnomon (;0;0;0;0) that carry the
    // highlights, since a raised filled region would cover its neighbours
    // (#140) — the arc owns the name UVW, so captions reach the region with
    // {UVW|UVWg}; transparent segment targets (;0;0;0); solid twins DG, FI,
    // GK (initiallyHidden) so the annex strokes out from D and the parallels
    // down from F and G; a right-angle marker at P for the angle LPM.
    //
    // Joyce's text never draws the parallels (X.91's "Draw EH, FI, and GK"
    // has no counterpart here), so they stroke in on the slide where the
    // rectangles AI and FK are first named. "each of the rectangle AI by FK"
    // is his slip for "each of the rectangles AI and FK", left literal.
    //
